  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nClosed generic registrations (#336, closes #318 and #329). A closed registration such as typeof(IRepository\\<int>) now generates the open type's imposter, IRepositoryImposter\\<T>, as IMP006 and the docs already said:\n\nUnder C# 14 it failed to compile (CS9295), because its Imposter() extension was declared for IRepository\\<int>.\n\nRegistering one generic type more than once, closed and closed or closed and open, reported IMP007 and generated nothing. The registrations now share the one imposter, and each closed one still reports IMP006.\n\nChange: with putInTheSameNamespace: false, a closed registration's imposter now goes into the open type's namespace, such as Imposters.Sample.IRepository\\_T\\_ instead of Imposters.Sample.IRepository\\_int\\_.\n\nA type nested in a generic class keeps the containing type's type arguments: typeof(Outer\\<int>.Inner) generates as before and no longer reports IMP006.\n\nType parameters named like the imposter's own types (#338, closes #330). A target such as IRepo\\<GetDelegate>, whose type parameter has the name of a type the imposter generates, failed to compile. Those types are now renamed, as they already were for a member of that name.",
